WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.368
-Our next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.770
who created and stars
in the new comedy series

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.274
"The Ms. Pat Show,"
which is streaming now on BET+.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.642
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.176
-What's going on with you?

00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:12.679
-You wouldn't understand.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.779
-Why not?

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.049
-You don't care about
stuff like this.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.083
-Like what?

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.418
-Racism.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.953
You bought those Paula Deen pots

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.621
even after she called us
the N-word.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:24.791
-Child, them pots
went from $100 to $20.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.695
That's the best time
to buy racism,

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.996
when it's on sale.

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:36.469
Hell, I'm still waiting on
Rachael Ray to [bleep] up.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.671
-Please welcome to the show
Ms. Pat.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.107
Pat, how are you?
-Hey, how you doing?

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.541
-I'm doing really well.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:46.212
So, you got into comedy
a little bit later in life.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.814
What was it that made you decide

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:50.417
that comedy was the right career
for you?

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:53.887
-'Cause I'm a convicted felon
and it's hard to find a job.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.755
-Okay.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.624
-It was the only thing
that wouldn't ask me

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.191
for a criminal background
history.

00:00:59.191 --> 00:01:00.794
So I was like, "This is for me.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.029
Nobody care what I did
10 years ago."

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.498
-But you had --
when you started doing it,

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.367
you already had two kids,
you were married,

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.303
and when you started going out
to do comedy,

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.538
you actually were not straight
with your husband.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:16.175
You told him you were going out
and taking dancing lessons?

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.210
-Yeah, until my wigs came back

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.179
smelling like weed
and cigarettes.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.548
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.818
-He was like, "What type
of lessons are you taking,

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.685
coming home smelling like that?"

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:28.788
And I was like,
"Well, I'm a comedian."

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.624
He was like, "Please get a job.
Please get a job."

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.992
I'm like,
"No, it's something here.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.326
They say I'm funny,

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:37.496
and it don't require
a criminal background history."

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:39.365
And I just kept going.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:42.035
-Well, I'm sure he is glad
that you did.

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.970
I want to talk a little bit --
So, you grew up in Atlanta.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.307
Based on what I've heard,
maybe a rougher part of Atlanta.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.976
Is it true that --
I'm reading it here --

00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:54.947
you've been shot twice
and hit by a dump truck once?

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.382
-Yeah, I was shot twice,

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:59.152
once in the titty and once
in the back of the head.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.486
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:02.522
-The dump truck
came from an accident

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:05.291
with my first kid's father.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.293
And, you know, I've learned
to live with a half a nipple.

00:02:08.293 --> 00:02:09.795
Two nipples is overrated.

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:12.364
Nobody's ever gonna use both
of them at the same time.

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:14.800
-[ Laughs ]
That's a very --

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.802
-And by the time I was shot
the second time,

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:18.104
there was no need
for the nipple.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:21.741
I didn't want to give my baby
lead poison anyway.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:25.010
-Now, this show
is about your life.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:26.779
It's based on the people
in your life.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.514
How does your family feel

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:32.251
about you using
these personal stories?

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:35.754
-What are they gonna say?
I get paid.

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:37.623
Who's gonna stop me?
I'm the mama.

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.124
[ Laughs ]

00:02:39.124 --> 00:02:43.295
If you don't want me to write
it, don't do it in front of me.

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:45.631
Nobody can stop me.

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:48.267
They cheering me
all the way to the bank.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:52.204
-This is based on you moving
from Atlanta to Indiana.

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:53.639
This was a real-life move
of yours.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:57.343
Did you experience culture shock
when you made that move?

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.611
-Oh, my God,
when I first got to Indiana,

00:02:59.611 --> 00:03:00.946
they had corn everywhere.

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:02.415
And I've never seen corn.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:03.850
I asked the Realtor, I was like,

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.018
"Why don't these people
cut they grass?"

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:08.421
He literally --

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.856
He pulled over and laughed at me
for 10 minutes.

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:12.125
He was like,
"Ma'am, that's corn."

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:15.461
I'm like,
"Why y'all got so much?"

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.229
And then I moved
into an apartment,

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:18.798
and my white neighbors

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.600
did something
my black neighbors never did.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.069
They knocked on the door
with a chocolate cake.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.403
And it floored me.

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:26.439
And I called my friend who live
in a white neighborhood,

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.274
and I was like,
"Uh, they bringing me food."

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.408
She was like, "Just eat it.

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:31.077
They don't want you
to break in they house."

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.113
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.515
And so -- which --

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:37.984
You know,
I'm from a black community.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.486
You don't knock on black people
door and bring them food.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.655
That's a sign of,
you want my husband.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:45.090
So that's why I was like,
"She want my husband?

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.526
We just moved here."

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:52.198
-Now, Pat, I heard in
the shooting of this show,

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.867
and it's never easy
to shoot a television show,

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.302
but it was
particularly hard on you

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.604
because you were
becoming dehydrated.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:02.875
I have heard, Pat,
you don't like to drink water.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.209
-I don't like water.

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:05.711
I grew up in the inner city
of Atlanta,

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:07.247
and they didn't care
what type of field trip

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.481
they took poor
little black kids to.

00:04:09.481 --> 00:04:11.216
So they took me
to the waterwork.

00:04:11.216 --> 00:04:14.053
And they took me on a part
where it was unprocessed

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.389
and said, "Hey, this is
how you make water."

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.624
And they scared
the crap out of me.

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:20.559
And then they took you
to the other side with a cup

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:22.161
and say,
"Take a cold glass of water."

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.163
I was like, "No,
I'm not gonna take --

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.899
I think I saw something
my brother put out there."

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.102
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:32.371
-And so I don't like water.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.039
I mean, they scared me.

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:36.308
So, I mean, I can't do it.

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:39.112
I should do it,
but I don't like water.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.180
But I do take a bath,
because I'm in my --

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.782
I'm over 40,

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.217
and I don't have the type of
body where you can skip a bath.

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:48.121
'Cause if I do, some items
are gonna start tapping on me,

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.690
"You need to go wash us, quick."

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.760
-Did you --
You know, you talked about

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.161
getting into comedy
later in life.

00:04:56.161 --> 00:04:58.897
What were some of the jobs
you had earlier in your life?

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:03.936
-Oh, I used to work
at McDonald's, Target, Walmart.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:07.140
I used to steal from McDonald's.
That was my side hustle.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.942
All teenagers stole
from McDonald's, okay?

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.677
The statute of limitations
is up.

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:13.078
Don't come after me, McDonald's.

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:16.582
So that was my side hustle,
stealing from McDonald's.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.084
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:19.084 --> 00:05:21.921
-You -- Not only do you
have your new show,

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.757
you're gonna start touring
again, which is so exciting,

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.726
and you have a podcast,
"The Patdown,"

00:05:27.726 --> 00:05:31.330
and you've managed to do that
through the pandemic?

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.433
-Oh, yeah, I do "The Patdown"
right there.

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:35.001
I have a movie theater
in the bottom of my room

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.869
and I can go down there, no wig.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:37.970
They don't care how I look.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.672
They just want me to talk, Seth.

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.274
And it's a nice little room.

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:42.875
I can get away from my husband
and my kids.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.344
A lot of times the whole family
interrupt the podcast,

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:48.080
so I put everybody
on the podcast.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.217
-Are you excited to get out
and start touring again?

00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:54.787
-Yeah, you know, when you're
married to the same person,

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:55.955
you leave them a little while,

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:57.957
you come home,
you love them a little bit more.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:00.159
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.361
I know you can't say that,
but I can say that

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:03.830
'cause he won't see this.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.965
He's asleep.
He go to sleep at 5:00.

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:08.200
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.635
Well, I can imagine.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.704
I can imagine he needs
a good night's sleep.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.640
Hey, Pat,
congratulations on the show.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.142
And thanks so much
for spending time with us.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.909
It's been a delight
talking to you.

00:06:17.909 --> 00:06:20.079
-Thank you for having me.

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.715
-"The Ms. Pat Show"
is streaming on BET+.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.816
And for information
on stand-up tour dates,

00:06:24.816 --> 00:06:26.619
go to mspatcomedy.com.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.221
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

